y the pipeline itself).\n3. Make the report generation write out report.md documenting the versions.\n\nDesign of the selection logic within analysis.py:\n\n```\nHIGH_LOF_INTOLERANT: use gnomAD constraint from work/constraint_raw.json (fetched on 2026-08-27):\n  - STXBP1: LOEUF=0.0987, pLI=1.0, obs/exp 3/78.5, lof_z=7.23\n  - OR1J1: no data (flag no_exp_lof)\nSelection criteria:\n  a. Stop_gained consequence in a protein_coding gene\n  b. High-confidence mosaic filters (already applied in calling)\n  c. LoF-intolerant gene: LOEUF < 0.35 AND pLI >= 0.9 (standard thresholds)\n  d. AF <= 0.45 to exclude germline heterozygous (OR1J1's 0.4615 fails c anyway)\n```\n\nThen write out the outputs. allele_fraction: report 4 decimal places (0.1935). Columns of variant.tsv exactly: chrom, pos, ref, alt, gene, consequence, alt_reads, total_reads, allele_fraction.\n\nContents of evidence.json — comprehensive. report.md — narrative.\n\nRegarding the constraint JSON file: work/constraint_raw.json contains the raw response strings; parse them within analysis.py to extract the values; for self-containedness, also embed a fallback copy of the numbers in analysis.py (documented: retrieved from the gnomAD API on 2026-08-27).\n\nFirst, try dbSNP once more (quickly), then write the final section of analysis.py."}}
