{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_103","type":"reasoning","text":"According to dbSNP (NCBI), no known SNP exists at either position (both empty) — meaning both are novel/novel variants, and STXBP1 c.349G>T is not a documented common germline polymorphism, which is consistent with it being a rare mosaic variant. Note: dbSNP not being found could also be due to limitations of the query, but this is recorded as-is.\n\nWait — the context around position 127661125: \"GATGCCCTGTTTAATGAACTGGTAAAATCCC\", with the caret at index 15 → base at position p = ref[15] = 'G' ✓. Hmm, interesting: looking at \"...TTTAATGAA...\" — wait, let me recount: sequence from p-16: positions p-16..p+14: G A T G C C C T G T T T A A T G A A C T G G T A A A A T C C C. p-16+15 = p-1 → index 15 = 'G'? Index: 0:G,1:A,2:T,3:G,4:C,5:C,6:C,7:T,8:G,9:T,10:T,11:T,12:A,13:A,14:T,15:G ✓ p='G'. Good. Codon context on the transcript (+ strand): c.349 = 1st position of codon; codon = GAA: bases at c.349-351 = G A A → the reference immediately after G at position p should be 'AA': the indices following p are 'A','A' ✓ (indices 16,17 = A,A).\n\nFor OR1J1 (- strand), the position is TGC→TGA at c.705 (transcript) — no issue.\n\nNow let's finalize analysis.py:\n1. Fix the frame check: frame_expected = (3 - cc%3) % 3.\n2. Add a selection + output generation section that deterministically writes out variant.tsv / evidence.json / report.md.\n\nUpdate main() to perform selection and output. The constraint data will be loaded from work/constraint_raw.json (obtained from the gnomAD API), with a fallback to the embedded copy.\n\nAlso, record in evidence the independent verification counts (raw overlap count 94, counts including the unfiltered base) — computed within the script by a small recount function at the selected site (all primary overlapping reads without quality filters, then after filtering) — essentially a re-verification.\n\nNow let's write the final version of analysis.py. Rewrite the entire file cleanly (this time carefully):\n\nSections:\n- Header docstring (versions)\n- Constants and filters\n- Helpers (log, load_reference, parse_cigar)\n- pileup (existing, correct)\n- call_candidates (existing)\n- parse_gtf, build_transcript, cds_coord_of (existing)\n- annotate_candidates (existing)\n- write_candidate_table (existing, using c.get)\n- fix frame_check → (3 - cc%3)%3\n- New: verify_site(sam_path, pos, ref, alt) → independent recount (all primary overlapping reads + filtered)\n- New: load_constraint() → parses work/constraint_raw.json; returns a dict symbol -> {loeuf, pli, obs_lof, exp_lof, lof_z, flags}\n- New: select_variant(nonsense, constraint) → applies the high LoF-intolerant criterion (LOEUF<0.35 & pLI>=0.9) + AF<=0.45, ranks, returns the best + decision log\n- New: write_outputs(selected, cands, nonsense, stats, constraint, ref_seq, verify)\n  - variant.tsv (exact columns)\n  - evidence.json\n  - report.md\n- main() orchestrates everything.\n\nRegarding HGVS: the selected variant in the canonical transcript ENST00000373302.8 (the highest-version-numbered basic? The canonical STXBP1 in MANE is ENST00000373302 (v8)). Actually, let's check which STXBP1 transcript is MANE Select — does the GTF have tag \"MANE_Select\"? My parse_gtf stores tags; I saw tags like ['CCDS'], ['basic'], ['GENCODE_Primary'] but none were MANE_Select. Hmm — this chr9 GTF subset may not contain MANE tags (or STXBP1's MANE Select = ENST00000373302, tag MANE_Select — but the list of observed tags for ENST00000373302.8 was ['CCDS']). Interesting: tags attribute in GTF: \"tag \\\"CCDS\\\"; tag \\\"basic\\\";\" — multiple tag attributes! My parser stores attr['tag'] = last value (the dict overwrites). So the tags list is incomplete. Fix: collect multiple values for 'tag'. Minor point, but let's fix the parsing to collect all values per key (tags as a list). Then check for the presence of the MANE_Select tag.\n\nAlso on canonical selection: report the representative transcript = longest CDS among basic/CCDS, or the one with the highest version of ENST00000373302.8 if it exists.\n\nSo, let's write the complete final analysis.py file. Long but straightforward. Write it as a PowerShell here-string. Need to be careful that '@ is placed at the start of a line, and that the content doesn't contain a leading '@ at line start.\n\nThe report.md content will be generated from the data with all numbers embedded. Let's carefully draft everything.\n\nAlso: evidence.json should include:\n{\n  \"task\": \"...\",\n  \"generated\": ISO date,\n  \"reference\": {\"assembly\":\"GRCh38\",\"contig\":\"chr9\",\"source\":\"Broad GATK resource bundle (Homo_sapiens_assembly38)\",\"length\":138394717,\"file\":\"inputs/reference/GRCh38_chr9.fa.gz\"},\n  \"annotation\": {\"source\":\"GENCODE v47 primary assembly\",\"file\":\"inputs/reference/gencode.v47.chr9.annotation.gtf.gz\",\"protein_coding_transcripts\":2998},\n  \"reads\": {\"file\":\"inputs/deleterious.mutation.q2.R1.fq.gz\",\"total_reads\":431396,\"read_length_max\":151,\"aligned_primary\":427460,\"used_mapq_ge_20\":417753,\"covered_positions\":15991973},\n  \"alignment\": {\"aligner\":\"minimap2 2.31-r1302\",\"preset\":\"-x sr\",\"command\":\"minimap2 -ax sr -t 14 work/ref/GRCh38_chr9.fa inputs/deleterious.mutation.q2.R1.fq.gz\"},\n  \"filters\": {...},\n  \"variant\": {...all details...},\n  \"constraint\": {...gnomAD values, source URL, access date...},\n  \"rejected_alternatives\": [OR1J1 + reasons],\n  \"validation\": {independent recount numbers, dbSNP query results},\n  \"candidate_summary\": {\"total_candidates\":328,\"stop_gained_candidates\":2}\n}\n\nAlso, note that total FASTQ read count 431396 was computed earlier; the script can compute this cheaply by reading the gzipped fastq (1.4s) — include it for reproducibility.\n\nReport.md sections: Objective, Input and versions, Methods (alignment, pileup filters, calling criteria, annotation, constraint evidence, selection), Results (variant table, HGVS, AF), Evidence for mosaicism, Evidence for LoF intolerance, Excluded candidates, Validation, Limitations, Files.\n\nOne decision: consequence string in variant.tsv = \"stop_gained\".\n\nAllele fraction: 18/93 = 0.193548... → round to 4 decimal places as 0.1935.\n\nLet me also double-check that ENST00000373302.8 is indeed the canonical STXBP1 transcript (highest version, basic tag, length 603aa). Yes, and it's also the longest (cds 1809).\n\nMANE: let me check the MANE_Select tag in the GTF for STXBP1 after fixing multi-tag parsing. If present, report that transcript as the representative. (STXBP1's MANE Select is ENST00000373302.9 in newer GENCODE; v47 might be .8.)\n\nSo, let's write the final file. Given the length, split into two here-string appends.\n"}}
