n, and finalize.\n\nAlso, one more consideration about \"consequence\" in variant.tsv — \"stop_gained\" is the standard SO term ✓.\n\nAlso, should I check for any other potential stop-gained variants I missed due to the filters (e.g., alt=3, or AF<0.02)? Task: \"high-confidence mosaic nonsense SNV\" — my thresholds are reasonable, but let me do a sanity scan: among candidates below the threshold, are there any stop-gained ones with moderate evidence (e.g., alt reads 2–3)? Simple check: relax to MIN_ALT>=2, AF>=0.01, and look for nonsense in LoF-intolerant genes. This is a robustness check, not part of the final filter. Let me quickly run it with an ad-hoc script that reuses the analysis module.\n"}}
